  tocontrolsame-orderforcing, thenratio, thenentry. Normalizedcurrentvector
  X_m\<less\>=Xfine/2+1/4 givesperiod/historyuniformfiniteoutputbounds.

  <section|Review status and precise consequence><label|review-status-and-precise-consequence>

  Independent review confirmed the displayed maps/norms; actual transferred
  currents meettheweightedbound/freejet/vanishingdefect hypotheses
  of17regulatorcompletion. This removes the current-regulator suppliergap. It
  does NOT automatically prove the separate marked
  finitecoefficient/traceprimitive endpoint rates or prescribed-radius
  comparison acrossstageboundaries; those require their own matching to11/13.
  No target\<minus\>12\<kappa\>isusedasinput.

  No newbibliography: gauge-local Taylor characterization already attributed
  in7; exactfinitealgebra andhomogeneousestimates derivedhere. No
  globalbuild.

  The stress low-jet preservation now explicitly separates one nonprincipal
  alias (order two plus at least one principal Ward momentum, hence order
  three) from two nonprincipal aliases (order four). Only the principal pair
  affects the weight-four stress coefficient.
